---
import "../styles/global.css";

const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Engrams is the Schema Runtime for AI agents. It isn't a passive memory store or static markdown rules — it's an active runtime that finds, defines, and refines mental models like the human brain."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Engrams — The Schema Runtime for AI Agents</title>
  </head>
  <body class="runtime-body">
    <!-- ── TOP BAR ── -->
    <header class="top-bar">
      <div class="bar-inner">
        <a href="/" class="brand">
          <span class="glyph">⬡</span>
          <span class="name">ENGRAMS</span>
          <span class="version">v0.14.0</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav">
          <a href="#what">What is a Schema</a>
          <a href="#runtime">Why a Runtime</a>
          <a href="#lifecycle">How It Learns</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="highlight">Guide</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="page-content">
      <!-- ══ 1. THE HERO ══ -->
      <section class="hero-section">
        <h1 class="hero-title">
          The Schema Runtime<br />
          <span class="accent">for AI Coding Agents.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          Static markdown rules bloat your prompt. Flat memory stores sit passively waiting to be queried.
          Engrams is an <strong>active runtime</strong> that continuously finds, defines, and refines
          mental models for your codebase — just like the human brain.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">5-Minute Quick Start</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action secondary">Read the Schema Guide</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 2. WHY A RUNTIME? (CATEGORICAL SEPARATION) ══ -->
      <section id="runtime" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Why a Schema Runtime?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Other tools treat AI context as static text files or dead database records. A runtime is fundamentally different:
          it actively perceives changes, clusters patterns, and executes directives at the exact point of action.
        </p>

        <div class="runtime-matrix">
          <div class="matrix-card">
            <h3>Vector Databases &amp; ADR Lists (Passive)</h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw">Dead history waiting to be searched</div>
            <p>
              Stores hundreds of isolated notes. But the agent has no trigger condition — it doesn't know
              <em>when</em> a rule applies. It either queries blindly or ignores your history completely.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-card">
            <h3>Prompt Stuffing &amp; <code>.cursorrules</code> (Static)</h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw">Brittle, manual, and bloated</div>
            <p>
              Developers manually write rigid text rules that get dumped into every prompt regardless of relevance.
              Consumes context window space and causes severe attention decay in reasoning models.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-card matrix-featured">
            <h3>The Engrams Runtime (Active Schemas)</h3>
            <div class="matrix-flaw text-burgundy">Continuous perception &amp; 1ms execution</div>
            <p>
              Autonomously clusters codebase activity, formalizes triggers and directives, and intercepts agent
              edits in 1ms with compact mental models.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 3. WHAT IS A SCHEMA? ══ -->
      <section id="what" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">What is a Schema?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          A schema is not a mechanical compiler rule. A compiler rule says <em>"don't clone on line 42."</em>
          A Cognitive Schema is an <strong>intuitive mental model</strong> that packages multiple decisions,
          code conventions, and tools into a single working paradigm.
        </p>

        <!-- Real Specimen 1: Performance Rules (Engineering Paradigm) -->
        <div class="specimen-card">
          <div class="sc-header">
            <div class="sc-title">
              <span class="sc-badge">SCHEMA 01</span>
              <code>performance-rules</code>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-meta-group">
              <span class="sc-status">● active · guided 14 sessions</span>
              <span class="sc-centroid">centroid: performance: 4 · sql: 1 · src/ops: 4</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sc-content">
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">⚡ MENTAL TRIGGER</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>When does this mental model activate?</strong>
                <p>Fires whenever I edit Rust code that creates, copies, or hands off collections and strings</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">📋 CONCEPTUAL DIRECTIVE</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What operational paradigm is enforced?</strong>
                <p class="rule-box">
                  The four allocation rules (no throwaway collections, borrow SQL params, keep borrowed strings borrowed, consume lookup maps) plus the checker that enforces them.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">🔗 BUNDLED MEMBERS</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What decisions, patterns, and code anchors are unified?</strong>
                <div class="sc-members">
                  <span class="m-pill">Decision #88: Borrowed SQL parameter lists</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Decision #91: Static vocabulary returns Cow&lt;str&gt;</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Pattern #11: Single-source row projections</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Pattern #12: Enrich by move, not get().clone()</span>
                  <span class="m-pill checker">Checker: engrams check --staged</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/ops/schemas/retrieval.rs</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/ops/schemas/list.rs</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Real Specimen 2: What to Build Next (Strategic Planning) -->
        <div class="specimen-card" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
          <div class="sc-header">
            <div class="sc-title">
              <span class="sc-badge badge-rose">SCHEMA 02</span>
              <code>what-to-build-next</code>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-meta-group">
              <span class="sc-status">● active · guided 16 sessions</span>
              <span class="sc-centroid">centroid: roadmap: 1 · planning: 1 · versioning: 1</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sc-content">
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">⚡ MENTAL TRIGGER</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>When does this mental model activate?</strong>
                <p>Fires when planning releases, evaluating roadmap priorities, or drafting new feature specifications</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">📋 CONCEPTUAL DIRECTIVE</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What operational paradigm is enforced?</strong>
                <p class="rule-box warm">
                  The pack that answers "what should engrams do next?": the 2026 agent-memory research survey (8 saved findings), the decision that turned it into a tiered version-by-version roadmap, and the survey session note. My learn → plan → ship loop — read this before writing any new spec.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">🔗 BUNDLED MEMBERS</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What decisions, research, and progress notes are unified?</strong>
                <div class="sc-members">
                  <span class="m-pill">Decision #74: Tiered version roadmap</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Research: 2026 agent-memory survey (8 findings)</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Progress: Survey session notes &amp; synthesis</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: specs/</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contrast-callout">
          <h3>Why this is a mental model, not a linter rule</h3>
          <p>
            Notice how both schemas capture <strong>how an expert thinks</strong>: 
            <code>performance-rules</code> doesn't just block a single function call; it packages four architectural decisions, two code files, and a validation checker into an instant zero-allocation posture. 
            <code>what-to-build-next</code> packages a research survey and roadmap decisions into a planning protocol. 
            Your AI receives the complete mental model on Turn 1 before writing a single line of code.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 4. HOW THE RUNTIME LEARNS: FINDS, DEFINES, REFINES, EXECUTES ══ -->
      <section id="lifecycle" class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">How the Runtime Learns</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          The human brain doesn't require manual file editing to form intuition. Engrams runs a continuous
          cognitive loop: perceiving clusters, defining boundaries, adapting to drift, and executing just in time.
        </p>

        <div class="loop-grid">
          <!-- Step 1: Finds -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <h3>1. Finds</h3>
            <p>
              As you commit code and log decisions, graph community detection identifies natural clusters
              of co-edited files and decisions in local SQLite.
            </p>
            <div class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema scan</code></div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2: Defines -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <h3>2. Defines</h3>
            <p>
              At session close, Engrams nudges you with ready-to-run confirm commands, and authoring enforces
              strict trigger-and-rule contracts.
            </p>
            <div class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema confirm decision:88 --name performance-rules</code></div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3: Refines -->
          <div class="loop-card">
            <h3>3. Refines</h3>
            <p>
              Tracks git staleness drift, records retrieval surface counts, and re-notifies when new candidate
              evidence advances beyond prior notifications.
            </p>
            <div class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams schema refine performance-rules --trigger "..." --rule "..."</code></div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 4: Executes -->
          <div class="loop-card lc-featured">
            <h3>4. Executes</h3>
            <p>
              Tomorrow, your AI touches matching files. <code>engrams advise</code> intercepts the edit in 1ms,
              injecting the active schema before a single line is written.
            </p>
            <div class="lc-code"><code>$ engrams advise src/ops/schemas/retrieval.rs</code></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 5. THREE COMMANDS THAT RUN IT ══ -->
      <section class="content-section">
        <h2 class="section-heading">Three Operational Levers</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Your AI executes the advice automatically. You steer the runtime with three high-leverage commands.
        </p>

        <div class="cmd-stack">
          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams advise src/ops/schemas/retrieval.rs</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "schemas": [
    &#123;
      "id": 1,
      "name": "performance-rules",
      "summary": "Fires whenever I edit Rust code that creates, copies, or hands off collections...",
      "guided": 14
    &#125;
  ],
  "constraints": [ ... ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams schema show performance-rules</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "name": "performance-rules",
  "summary": "Fires whenever I edit Rust code that creates, copies, or hands off collections...",
  "guided": 14,
  "members": [
    &#123;"kind": "decision", "id": 88, "summary": "Borrowed SQL parameter lists"&#125;,
    &#123;"kind": "decision", "id": 91, "summary": "Static vocabulary returns Cow"&#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="cmd-box">
            <div class="cb-chrome">
              <span class="cb-cmd">$ engrams session close --pr 42</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="cb-body"><code>&#123;
  "schema_value": &#123;"guided_retrievals": 6, "distinct_schemas": 2&#125;,
  "schema_opportunities": [
    &#123;"confirm_command": "engrams schema confirm decision:88 --name performance-rules"&#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 6. INSTALL ══ -->
      <section class="install-section">
        <div class="install-box">
          <h2>Give your AI the mental models it deserves.</h2>
          <p>Local SQLite engine. 0MB background memory. 1ms query execution.</p>
          <div class="install-code">
            <code>cargo install engrams-cli</code>
            <span class="sep">or</span>
            <code>brew install stevebrownlee/tap/engrams</code>
          </div>
          <div class="install-actions">
            <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">5-Minute Quick Start</a>
            <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action secondary">Read the Full Guide</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- ── FOOTER ── -->
    <footer class="bottom-footer">
      <div class="footer-wrap">
        <span class="footer-brand">⬡ ENGRAMS · Apache-2.0 · The Schema Runtime for AI Agents</span>
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas">Cognitive Schemas</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="/docs/reference/cli">CLI Reference</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     COOLORS PALETTE (LIGHTER BACKGROUNDS, DARKER TEXT):
     #ffd9da (Pale Rose / Blush) | #ea638c (Vibrant Rose) |
     #89023e (Deep Burgundy)     | #30343f (Deep Slate)   | #1b2021 (Night)
     Zero black background. Zero tiny headers. Sizing fixed.
     ============================================================ */

  :root {
    --c-rose-pale:   #ffd9da; /* soft warm blush / light accent background */
    --c-rose:        #ea638c; /* vibrant rose / active accent */
    --c-burgundy:    #89023e; /* deep rich burgundy / primary button / focus */
    --c-slate:       #30343f; /* secondary dark slate text */
    --c-night:       #1b2021; /* primary deep dark text (16:1 contrast) */
    --c-white:       #ffffff;
    --c-surface-subtle: #fff8f8;
    --c-border:      #ffd9da;
    --c-border-strong: #ea638c;
    --font-mono: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  .runtime-body {
    background: var(--c-white);
    color: var(--c-night);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  /* ── TOP BAR ── */
  .top-bar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  }
  .bar-inner {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--c-night); }
  .glyph { color: var(--c-burgundy); font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 900; }
  .name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 900; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--c-night); }
  .version { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--c-rose); margin-left: 0.2rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .nav { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .nav a { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--c-slate); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; transition: color 0.15s; }
  .nav a:hover { color: var(--c-burgundy); }
  .nav a.highlight { color: var(--c-burgundy); font-weight: 800; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .nav a:not(:last-child):not(.highlight) { display: none; } }

  /* ── MAIN CONTENT CONTAINER ── */
  .page-content {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 7rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  /* ── 1. HERO ── */
  .hero-section {
    margin-bottom: 5.5rem;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.8vw, 4.4rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--c-night);
    margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
  }
  .hero-title .accent {
    color: var(--c-burgundy);
    display: block;
  }
  .hero-lede {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--c-slate);
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
  }
  .hero-lede strong { color: var(--c-night); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* ── TECHNICAL BUTTONS (SHARP RECTANGULAR, ZERO PILLS) ── */
  .btn-action {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.6rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 2px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-action.primary {
    background: var(--c-burgundy);
    color: #ffffff;
    border-color: var(--c-burgundy);
  }
  .btn-action.primary:hover {
    background: #6a0130;
    border-color: #6a0130;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(137, 2, 62, 0.35);
  }
  .btn-action.secondary {
    background: var(--c-white);
    color: var(--c-burgundy);
    border-color: var(--c-burgundy);
  }
  .btn-action.secondary:hover {
    background: var(--c-rose-pale);
    color: #550126;
  }

  /* ── COMMON SECTION HEADERS (NO TINY LABELS) ── */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
    padding-top: 3.5rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--c-rose-pale);
  }
  .section-heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--c-night);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .section-description {
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    color: var(--c-slate);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.8rem;
  }
  .section-description strong { color: var(--c-night); }

  /* ── 2. RUNTIME MATRIX (THREE-WAY SPLIT) ── */
  .runtime-matrix {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .matrix-card {
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    padding: 2rem 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .matrix-featured {
    border: 2px solid var(--c-rose);
    background: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(234, 99, 140, 0.12);
  }
  .matrix-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-night);
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .matrix-flaw {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--c-slate);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .text-burgundy { color: var(--c-burgundy); }
  .text-rose { color: var(--c-rose); }
  .matrix-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--c-slate);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .matrix-card strong { color: var(--c-night); }

  /* ── 3. WHAT IS A SCHEMA (SPECIMEN CARD) ── */
  .specimen-card {
    background: var(--c-white);
    border: 2px solid var(--c-border);
    border-radius: 2px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(27, 32, 33, 0.06);
  }
  .sc-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--c-surface-subtle);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sc-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .sc-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    background: var(--c-burgundy);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .sc-badge.badge-rose {
    background: var(--c-rose);
  }
  .sc-title code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-night);
  }
  .sc-meta-group { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sc-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--c-burgundy);
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .sc-centroid {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--c-slate);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .sc-content { padding: 2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .sc-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: baseline; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .sc-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; } }
  .sc-k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--c-burgundy);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .sc-v strong { display: block; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--c-slate); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .sc-v p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--c-night); line-height: 1.6; }
  .sc-v code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--c-burgundy); font-size: 0.9em; background: #fff0f2; padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .rule-box {
    font-family: var(--font-mono) !important;
    font-size: 0.94rem !important;
    background: #fff8f9;
    border: 1px solid var(--c-rose-pale);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-burgundy);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    color: var(--c-burgundy) !important;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .rule-box.warm {
    background: #fffbfa;
    border-color: #ffd9da;
